The solution is correct and clearly organized. It correctly counts:

- all 3-card hands as \(\binom{52}{3}=22100\);
- the paired rank and its two suits as \(13\binom42=78\);
- the third card as any of the \(48\) cards of a different rank.

Because the third card is explicitly chosen outside the pair’s rank, three-of-a-kind hands are excluded, as required. The final simplification
\[
\frac{3744}{22100}=\frac{72}{425}
\]
is also correct.

